the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the Alter of *a case* is *a number*; scenario element.
    the Geburtsjahr of *a case* is *a number*; scenario element.
    Volljährigkeit nachgewiesen holds for *a case*.
    Volljährigkeit nachgewiesen would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r4_3_accept_repeated_decision_id includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/accept-repeated-decision-id.ruml".

Volljährigkeit nachgewiesen holds for a case if
    the Alter of the case is a number N
    and N >= 18.

Volljährigkeit nachgewiesen holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Alter of the case is a number
    and the Geburtsjahr of the case is a number N
        and a number M = 2024 - N
        and M >= 18.

Volljährigkeit nachgewiesen holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Alter of the case is a number
    and it is not the case that the Geburtsjahr of the case is a second number
    and Volljährigkeit nachgewiesen would hold for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "accept-repeated-decision-id.ruml" at generated_1:
    % every data point its first value
    the Alter of case 1 is 18.
    the Geburtsjahr of case 1 is 2006.
    node_1 expects answers ["Volljährigkeit nachgewiesen holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers [].

